# World Model Inference — environment variable reference.
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in as needed. Nothing here is loaded automatically;
# these document the variables the deploy scripts, CDK app, and inference
# containers read. Export the ones you need before running ./deploy.sh, or set
# the WORLD_MODEL_* ones on the container/endpoint (SageMaker env, EC2 user
# data, `docker run -e`).

# ─── AWS / deploy-time (read by deploy.sh + CDK) ──────────────────────────────
# Target account + region. CDK also honours CDK_DEFAULT_ACCOUNT/REGION.
AWS_ACCOUNT_ID=123456789012
AWS_REGION=us-east-1

# Default model directory under inference/models/ (deploy.sh default arg).
# DEFAULT_MODEL=lingbot-fast

# Skip the interactive restricted-license prompt for gated models (e.g. Lyra-2).
# Set to 1 only if you accept the upstream model license.
# ACCEPT_LICENSE=0
# LYRA_LICENSE_ACK=0

# HuggingFace token for gated/private weight downloads (scripts/stage-weights.py).
# HF_TOKEN=hf_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# ACM certificate ARN → enables HTTPS on the EC2 ALB (passed as `-c certificateArn=`).
# CERTIFICATE_ARN=arn:aws:acm:us-east-1:123456789012:certificate/xxxxxxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxxxxxxxxxx

# ALB ingress CIDR. deploy.sh defaults to your own public IP (/32) so the
# endpoint isn't world-open. Set a range (e.g. your office/VPN) or explicitly
# 0.0.0.0/0 to expose the endpoint to the internet.
# ALLOWED_CIDR=203.0.113.0/24

# ─── Inference server security (read at container startup) ────────────────────
# Shared bearer token. When set, every non-health request must send
# `Authorization: Bearer <token>` (WebSockets: `?token=<token>`). When UNSET,
# the API is UNAUTHENTICATED and logs a startup warning.
#
# NOTE: ./deploy.sh AUTO-GENERATES this on first deploy and stores it in SSM
# (SecureString) at /world-model/security/api-token, then injects it into the
# EC2/SageMaker container and writes it into the frontend config. Set it here
# only to pin your own value instead of the generated one.
# WORLD_MODEL_API_TOKEN=change-me-to-a-long-random-string

# Comma-separated CORS allowlist (your CloudFront/frontend origin). When unset,
# cross-origin browser requests are denied (deny-by-default).
# WORLD_MODEL_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://d1234abcd.cloudfront.net

# Max requests per client IP per 60s on /generate and /invocations. 0 disables.
# WORLD_MODEL_RATE_LIMIT=60
